      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn ratios, proportions and simultaneous equations.\n\nThis lesson uses the methods and question patterns from the Simplification chapter.\n\nWe will keep each step small: understand one rule, see it with numbers, then try a similar question.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A ratio written as x/y = a/b can be turned into an equation by cross multiplication.\n\nbx = ay.\n\nExample: x/y = 3/5 means 5x = 3y. This form is easier to combine with another equation.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
